    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="section" id="takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>All regularization techniques penalize complexity</strong> — they constrain models toward simplicity, reducing overfitting at the cost of some training performance</li>
        <li><strong>L1 does feature selection, L2 shrinks evenly</strong> — choose based on whether you want automatic feature selection</li>
        <li><strong>Early stopping saves computation and prevents overfitting</strong> — monitor validation performance during training and stop when it plateaus</li>
        <li><strong>Ensemble methods reduce overfitting through diversity</strong> — averaging uncorrelated errors is one of the most powerful anti-overfitting techniques</li>
        <li><strong>Use validation curves to diagnose overfitting</strong> — they guide you toward the right hyperparameter settings that maximize generalization</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

